    "rules": [
     "League A (16 teams): the 12 lowest-ranked play a Swiss-style group stage in two groups of six, four matches each (two home, two away). The top two of each group join Mexico, USA, Canada and Panama (direct entry) in home-and-away quarter-finals in November 2026; aggregate winners reach the Finals at SoFi Stadium, Los Angeles. Fifth and sixth place are relegated to League B.",
     "League B (16 teams): four groups of four, home and away, six matches per team across the September-October and November windows. Group winners are promoted to League A and reach the League B Championship; fourth-placed teams are relegated to League C.",
     "League C (9 teams): three groups of three, each team plays every group opponent twice (four matches). Group winners and the best second-placed team are promoted to League B and reach the League C Championship.",
     "The 2026/27 Nations League serves as the qualifiers for the 2027 Concacaf Gold Cup."
    ],
